namespace pdg { /**

\fn pdg::NetConnection::sendDgram(NetworkData message)
\brief Send binary bytes or JSON data to the remote endpoint over an available unreliable transport.

Messages use UDP when available. Delivery and arrival order are not guaranteed; include a sequence number when newer updates supersede older ones. PDG handles packet framing.

\param message A Uint8Array (including Node Buffer), a JSON-compatible object or
array, or null. See \ref pdg::NetworkData for the complete contract.

Uint8Array inputs use binary serialization. Only the view's bytes are copied,
respecting byteOffset and byteLength. The receiver gets a Node Buffer on the
current Node-based networking runtimes. Plain objects, arrays and null use JSON
serialization; they must be JSON-compatible and contain no circular references.

Strings, MemBlock and ISerializable instances have separate overloads. Top-level
numbers and booleans are not accepted by this method.

\return The receiver for call chaining.

\see sendDgram(string)
\see sendDgram(MemBlock)
\see sendDgram(ISerializable)

WebTransport uses session datagrams after handshake completion. Payloads larger than its confirmed datagram limit, disabled/unavailable datagrams, or rejected datagram writes use the reliable stream. Native UDP falls back to TCP above 1492 serialized bytes. WebSocket always uses reliable delivery. A successful datagram write still has no delivery guarantee.

**/ }
